### 13. Read the reservation of request 6 — expect 200, unit "Held"
GET {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}

### 14. Confirm it — expect 200, unit "Confirmed"
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Confirmations

### 15. Confirm again — expect 200, no change
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Confirmations

### 16. Release the confirmed reservation — expect 409, code 16410
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Releases

### 17. Cancel the confirmed unit — expect 200, unit "Cancelled"
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Cancellations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "unitRefs": [ "{{hold.response.body.data.units[0].unitRef}}" ] }

### 18. Confirm after the cancellation — expect 409, code 16408
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Confirmations

### 19. A second reservation, then release it — expect 200 "Held", then 200 "Released"
# @name hold2
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "proof-2b-6",
  "reference": "proof-order-1",
  "expiresAt": "{{future}}",
  "context": {
    "currencyId": {{currencyId}},
    "asOf": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
    "travellers": [ { "ref": "T1", "passengerTypeCode": "ADT", "flightRefs": ["F1"] } ],
    "bounds": [ { "ref": "B1", "flights": [
      { "ref": "F1", "flightId": "100", "originAirportId": 1, "destinationAirportId": 2,
        "departureDateTime": "2027-01-10T08:00:00+03:30", "marketingAirlineId": {{airlineId}}, "operatingAirlineId": {{airlineId}} } ] } ],
    "existing": []
  },
  "units": [
    { "unitReference": "U1", "productRef": "XBAG1", "productVersion": 1, "priceRuleId": "{{rule.response.body.data.id}}", "travellerRef": "T1", "boundRef": "B1", "flightRef": null, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

###
POST {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/{{hold2.response.body.data.reservationId}}/Releases

### 20. An unknown reservation — expect 404, code 16401
GET {{host}}/Service/v1/ServiceReservations/1

### 21. Read the product — expect "lastUpdateTime" is NOT required in this response; instead check in SQL:
###     SELECT MAX(LastUpdateTime), COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT LastUpdateTime FROM ReadModel.AncillaryProducts
###     UNION ALL SELECT LastUpdateTime FROM ReadModel.AncillaryPriceRules) s;
###     Note the result, run request 22, and run the query again: the result must differ.
GET {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/AncillaryProducts/{{bag.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Suspend the product — expect 200, "Suspended" (and the stamp of request 21 changes)
POST {{host}}/Backoffice/v1/AncillaryProducts/{{bag.response.body.data.id}}/Suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
